# Non-source files used in MSW
# .codeblock/.directory/.scriptfile are tracked (not ignored): MSW Maker regenerates
# them locally with fresh random GUIDs on a clean clone, but .behaviourtree/.stateset
# files hardcode references to those GUIDs (definitionId/ScriptStateTypeId). Ignoring
# them let every clone silently diverge from what those files expect, breaking every
# node/state reference project-wide. Tracking them keeps the GUIDs stable across clones.
#*.codeblock
#*.directory
#*.scriptfile
#*.model
#*.userdataset

